building cloud-native applications can  often be difficult setting up the right  environments  accessing client libraries and figuring  out an easy way to deploy and debug your  application is time-consuming  to help you solve these challenges we  built cloud code cloud code is a set of  ide plugins that allows you to write  deploy and debug cloud native  applications quickly and  easily cloud code supports a number of  ides including visual studio code  jetbrains ide such as intellij and cloud  shell editor this way you can leverage  the tools you already know  let's dive deeper into how cloud code  helps you write deploy and debug your  code faster  first a collection of starter templates  showing best practices in a variety of  languages are available out of the box  and you can run these on google  kubernetes engine or cloud run with just  a few clicks  as you build out your app you can easily  enable and integrate numerous google  cloud apis from your ide  you can also leverage cloud code secret  manager integration to access  and manage sensitive data like api keys  passwords  and certificates right from your ide and  if you aren't someone who loves writing  yaml files  cloud code improves your yaml authoring  experience with features like code  snippets and inline documentation  once you're done writing your code and  those pesky yaml files it's time to  deploy  if you're trying to run your kubernetes  application on a local kubernetes  cluster cloud code makes it easy to  deploy to docker desktop or we'll create  and start a mini q cluster for you if  you don't have one  when developing cloud code can  automatically rebuild and redeploy your  code every time you make a change  it even supports hot reloading  individual files that change to the  container without a rebuild or redeploy  so you see updates in under a second  even better cloud code works with any  kubernetes cluster  be it on google cloud or any other cloud  after deploying you may discover issues  in your application  cloud code is here to help by providing  the same debugging experience you're  used to in the ide  even when debugging a remote kubernetes  cluster or a serverless application  just place breakpoints then debug your  code in your kubernetes cluster or  locally on cloud run emulator  if you need to dive deeper cloud code  also comes with a built-in log viewer to  help you monitor and debug issues with  your kubernetes and cloud run services  right within your ide now you know how  cloud code works to improve your  experience creating cloud-native  applications  within your favorite ide by helping you  write deploy and debug your code faster  we hope this short introduction to cloud  code gives you all you need to get  started  cloud code is the most productive way to  build cloud-native applications  and you can give it a try by going to  cloud.google.com forward slash code  also you can reach out to us via slack  you can find us using this link with  cloud dash code as the channel name
 

